
  <sn><md>### Rclone Architecture and Terminology

Rclone is designed around a **frontend command-line interface**, a **storage backend layer**, and the **remote storage provider**. This architecture allows the same commands such as `copy`, `sync`, `move`, and `mount` to work with many different storage systems.

**Architecture**

![diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/Programming/rclone/01.Introduction%20to%20RClone/assets/rclone_architecture.png)

+++ view ascii code

```text
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │       User          │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │    Rclone CLI       │
                    │  copy / sync / etc. │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │   Rclone Core       │
                    │                     │
                    │ • File operations   │
                    │ • Filtering         │
                    │ • Transfers         │
                    │ • Checksums         │
                    │ • Encryption        │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │   Storage Backend   │
                    │      (Remote)       │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
             ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐
             ▼                 ▼                 ▼
       Google Drive        Amazon S3         OneDrive
       Dropbox             WebDAV            SFTP
       MEGA                Azure             Local Disk
```
